  "autobiographical": [
    "Chronic neurotic anxiety at night, fear that 'they are going to come for me' — PKD's core paranoia.",
    "2-3-74 visions: he saw the Golden Fish; experienced shrewdness faculty coming online unexpectedly.",
    "Pentathol (likely sodium pentothal) administration during a crisis: PKD was hypnotized/abreacted, reliving childhood trauma.",
    "Receipt and analysis of the Xerox missive: a document (possibly military/espionage-related forgery) that triggered his fear response.",
    "Post-3-74: cessation of chronic night anxiety after abreaction—proof that he 'exorcised' the original trauma.",
    "Dreamed of working on his exegesis; integrated dream/waking visions.",
    "Parallelism: PKD's past life trauma (AD 70 Rome, death as Thomas) and present-day trap (modern security apparatus) forming a synchronistic pair."
  ],
